<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  FFT tool — port of Mirone's src_figs/fft_stuff.m (fft_stuff_LayoutFcn).

  The ARRANGEMENT is Mirone's, widget for widget and row for row: two framed boxes on top (the two
  grid pickers + Remove trend on the left, the padding size + its two good-FFT-number lists on the
  right), then CONFIRM, then the operations in columns — the three edit+Go rows on the left, the
  single-grid buttons, the two-grid buttons, and Analytic Signal.

  The NUMBERS are not Mirone's, and cannot be: MATLAB draws those captions in a narrower font, so
  the .m file's own widths ("Radial power average" in 121 px, "Up/Down Continuation" in 130) clip
  under Qt. Each widget is given the width its text really needs and the columns are spaced from
  those widths, so nothing overlaps and nothing is resized behind the user's back at runtime.
-->
<ui version="4.0">
